  "judgment": {
    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "Option 0 has a removable discontinuity at x=1: the two-sided limit is the height of the open circle, whereas f(1) is the different height of the filled point. MA's answer image depicts exactly this graph, with blue markers instead of red; the color change does not change the function. This confirms the earlier selection. All other choices are continuous at x=1, including those with corners.",
